     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Use <span data-math=\"C = \\frac{5}{9}\\left( {F - 32} \\right)\"></span> and <i>K</i> = <i>C</i> + 273 to find a Kelvin temperature given degrees Fahrenheit.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"K = C + {\\rm{ }}273\\;\"></span></p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"K = \\frac{5}{9}\\left( {F - 32} \\right) + 273\"></span></td>\n<td>Substitute the right side of the Fahrenheit to Celsius formula.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"K = \\frac{5}{9}\\left( {F-32} \\right) + 273\"> K = \\frac{5}{9}\\left( {F-32} \\right) + 273</span>"
